course: dictionary
lesson: 4348
title: Guilt and feelings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Guilt is a noun, and it names a feeling. It is the bad, uncomfortable feeling you have when you know you have done something wrong. Guilt can also mean the fact of having done something wrong, as in a court proving someone's guilt.
explain: Context helps you choose the right meaning. «Guilt about a hidden wrong usually grows each day it is not fixed; owning up is scary for a moment and then usually brings relief.» Here guilt is the uneasy feeling inside you, and it gets bigger until you put things right.
explain: «Guilt is the conscience working; it is a sign you know what is right, not proof you are a bad person.» Guilt is useful because it tells you to say sorry or fix a mistake. If you feel guilty about something that was not your fault, it does not help, so talk to someone you trust.
explain: Clue words such as feel, sense, conscience and wrong point to the feeling. Words such as court and proved point to the second meaning, about breaking a law.
fact: Guilt means the bad, uncomfortable feeling you have when you know you have done something wrong.
fact: Guilt can also mean having done something wrong or broken a law, as in «the court proved his guilt».
fact: Guilt is a normal emotion. It tells us to say sorry or put things right.
fact: Guilty is the adjective form of guilt, as in «feel guilty».
fact: Useful phrases: feel guilt, a sense of guilt, a guilty conscience. Guilt is uncountable, so we say some guilt, not a guilt.
exercise: «Guilt about a hidden wrong usually grows each day it is not fixed.» What does guilt mean here? | The sound of a bell | *The bad feeling you get when you know you did wrong | A type of weather | A prize for being good
exercise: «The court proved his guilt.» What does guilt mean in this sentence? | A sense of humour | *The fact of having done something wrong or broken a law | A long journey | A sweet, happy feeling
exercise: Which word is the adjective form of guilt? | *guilty | guilts | guilt
test: «Guilt is the conscience working; it is a sign you know what is right.» What does this sentence tell us about guilt? | *That it shows you know what is right | That you are sleepy | That you are a bad person | That you have no feelings at all
test: Which is the best advice for guilt about something you did wrong? | Hide it and never think about it again | Wait a year before doing anything | *Say sorry and put things right | Blame someone else
exam: Which is a correct phrase using guilt? | *a sense of guilt | a guilts of sense | guilt of a sense | a guilty of sense
